 ## Overview
-Face Visibility Check determines whether a specific voxel face needs to be meshed based on its own visibility state, the neighbor's visibility state, and whether the face has already been processed [S1, S2, unofficial]. It solves the problem of redundant geometry generation by culling hidden faces between two opaque full cubes; if two opaque cube faces touch, the internal faces do not need to be emitted into the mesh [S1, S2, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from sibling methods like [Culled Voxel Meshing](2392-culled-voxel-meshing.md) by focusing on the binary decision logic for full cubes rather than complex partial shape intersection or global visibility maps [S2, unofficial].
+Face Visibility Check determines whether a specific voxel face needs to be meshed based on its own visibility state, the neighbor's visibility state, and whether the face has already been processed [S1, unofficial]. It solves the problem of redundant geometry generation by culling hidden faces between two opaque full cubes; if two opaque cube faces touch, the internal faces do not need to be emitted into the mesh [S2, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from sibling methods like [Culled Voxel Meshing](2392-culled-voxel-meshing.md) by focusing on the binary decision logic for full cubes rather than complex partial shape intersection or global visibility maps [S2, unofficial].
 
