 ## Background
-Face culling in voxel rendering started with the simple observation that if two opaque cube faces touch, the internal faces do not need to be emitted [S2, unofficial]. The method was formalized in discussions around voxel cube culling and partial shapes, highlighting the limitations of boolean face solidity for non-cube shapes [S2, unofficial]. It is used in voxel meshing libraries such as `block-mesh-rs` and `mc-meshing` [S1, S3, unofficial].
+Face culling in voxel rendering started with the simple observation that if two opaque cube faces touch, the internal faces do not need to be emitted [S2, unofficial]. The method addresses the limitations of boolean face solidity for non-cube shapes, where a face may be partially covered by geometry [S2, unofficial].
 
